+## 0. Proof principles
+
+Evidence must observe the deployed behaviour it claims to prove. A capture or passing test only makes a claim eligible for independent judgment; it does not itself prove launch readiness. An unreachable flow is a recorded finding, not a skipped gate. The adversarial evaluator is independent of the author and is rewarded for finding a failure.
+
+## 1. Target Launch Platforms
+
+| Platform | Build artifact | Distribution |
+|---|---|---|
+| Web | versioned production web bundle and service deployment | HTTPS production deployment; hosting domain is intentionally not selected yet |
+
+### 1a. Promise Proof Map
+
+| Promise | Claim | Observable mechanism | Admissible evidence | Failure probe |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| PRM-001 | No reminder is scheduled before explicit confirmation of action text, owner, and due date. | The confirmation view exposes all three values; the scheduling boundary accepts only a confirmation bound to that complete payload and records the resulting reminder. | `live-probe:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/E001-reminder-confirmation/stories/S001-confirm-before-schedule/transcripts/<sha>-complete-confirmation.md@<sha>` plus baselined `db-catalog:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/E001-reminder-confirmation/stories/S001-confirm-before-schedule/logs/<sha>-reminder-readback.log@<sha>`. | Attempt scheduling with each field absent, with a stale confirmation after editing a field, and by calling the scheduling boundary directly; any reminder row or delivery attempt is a failure. |
+| PRM-002 | A workspace cannot read another workspace's transcript, action, or delivery status. | Every transcript, action, and delivery-status read is scoped by the authenticated workspace at the real authorization layer. | Paired real-principal reads, including an allowed principal and a different-workspace principal: `live-probe:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/E002-workspace-isolation/stories/S001-isolate-workspace-data/logs/<sha>-two-principal-reads.log@<sha>`. | Create data in workspace A, authenticate as workspace B, and try direct identifiers, list endpoints, and delivery-status polling. Any returned A data is a failure. |
+| PRM-003 | A confirmed reminder is delivered exactly once or exposes a truthful terminal failure state. | A confirmation creates one idempotent delivery record; attempts atomically transition it to delivered or a visible terminal-failure state. | Baseline and post-walk delivery-record reads: `db-catalog:specs/projects/001-pulseboard/epics/E003-reliable-delivery/stories/S001-idempotent-reminder-delivery/logs/<sha>-delivery-readback.log@<sha>`; a real provider callback or controlled provider failure is observed at the boundary. | Replay the same confirmation concurrently, retry after a timeout, and force provider rejection. More than one delivered event, a lost record, or a non-terminal silent failure is a failure. |
+
+## 2. Valid Proof Sources (per platform)
+
+### Platform: Web
+
+- A clean production build served in its production-like configuration, with the build SHA and sanitized environment captured.
+- Live requests against the deployed service or real runtime engine as named principals.
+- Pre-walk and post-walk datastore reads for persistence claims.
+- Baked-build screenshots, browser accessibility-tree dumps, and container-versus-content geometry measurements at 360px, 768px, and 1440px for UI fit claims.
+- An independently adjudicated cold-start LARP transcript for each primary job.
+
+### 2a. Claim admissibility
+
+| Claim type | Admissible | Does not count |
+|---|---|---|
+| correctness | tests, mutation guards, live probes, database reads, static checks, baked-build captures | none; the instrument must still exercise a real subject |
+| visibility | live reads as allowed and forbidden principals, datastore reads, device walk | mocked or bypass-capable clients, endpoint-shaped refusals, screenshots |
+| acceptance | request at deployed target or real engine, observed response | mocked client or hand-authored provider fixture without provenance |
+| persistence | pre-walk baseline plus post-walk datastore read-back | success screenshots or an unbaselined post-walk read |
+| fit | baked-build accessibility tree plus measured geometry at three widths | rule-engine pass, props assertion, jsdom layout, unmeasured screenshot |
+| behaviour | control-versus-treatment using the composed shipped prompt, with n reported | source assertion that a prompt string exists |
+
+### 2b. Typed citations and admissibility table
+
+A citation is `<type>:<path>@<sha>`. The closed types are `test`, `mutation-guard`, `live-probe`, `db-catalog`, `ax-dump`, `geometry`, `capture`, `device-walk`, `model-eval`, and `static`.
+
+| Claim type | Admissible citation types | Inadmissible here — and the scar that earned it |
+|---|---|---|
+| correctness | `test` `mutation-guard` `live-probe` `db-catalog` `static` `ax-dump` `geometry` `capture` `device-walk` `model-eval` | *(nothing — a green suite is the right and sufficient instrument for a correctness claim; this row can never fire)* |
+| visibility | `live-probe` `db-catalog` `device-walk` | `test` · `mutation-guard` — an anon-key server client carries no JWT, so `auth.uid() = <col>` returned **zero rows for every user, always**, silently. Two mutation-verified suites could not see it; a live read as each principal settled it in one query. Also `static`, `capture` |
+| acceptance | `live-probe` `db-catalog` `device-walk` | `test` — a **mocked client** encodes what we *believe* the deployment accepts, so it can only ever confirm our own belief. Only the real boundary can contradict it. Also `mutation-guard`, `static`, `capture` |
+| persistence | `live-probe` `db-catalog` | `capture` — a screenshot of a success state is not a written row; and a post-walk read with **no pre-walk baseline** cannot tell a fresh write from a stale seed. Also `test`, `mutation-guard`, `static` |
+| fit | `ax-dump` `geometry` `device-walk` | `test` — a **props-level a11y assertion** reads props, not the platform tree, and jsdom performs no layout. A rule engine is structurally blind to containment. Also `static`, `capture`, `mutation-guard` |
+| behaviour | `model-eval` `device-walk` | `static` — asserting the rule string is **present in the source** of a prompt is not evidence the composed prompt changed what the shipped model does. Also `test`, `capture` |
+
+## 3. Invalid Proof Sources (anti-proof)
+
+- A dev-server screenshot, source inspection, or a mock-only test cannot prove production delivery, authorization, or persistence.
+- A screenshot without adjudication cannot prove a user understood confirmation or a failure state.
+- A green test suite cannot claim SHIP, UX-RC, or COMMERCIAL-RC.
+- A skipped, empty, or bypass-capable-principal test cannot prove an authorization rule.
+
+## 4. Required Runtime LARP / Integration Stress Tests
+
+| Test | Persona / principal | Pass condition | Evidence home |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| First reminder, cold start | Team facilitator in workspace A | Can state the action, owner, due date, and consequence before confirming; no scheduling occurs before confirmation; independently adjudicated for DOES-IT-WORK and IS-IT-GOOD. | `epics/E001-reminder-confirmation/stories/S001-confirm-before-schedule/{screenshots,ax-trees,transcripts,logs}/<sha>-*` |
+| Cross-workspace hostile read | Facilitator A and facilitator B | A reads its own transcript/action/status; B cannot recover any A data through UI, identifiers, lists, or polling. | `epics/E002-workspace-isolation/stories/S001-isolate-workspace-data/logs/<sha>-two-principal-reads.log` |
+| Duplicate and failed delivery | Delivery worker plus provider failure fixture at the real boundary | Concurrent/replayed confirmation emits one delivery or one truthful terminal failure; no ambiguous pending state remains. | `epics/E003-reliable-delivery/stories/S001-idempotent-reminder-delivery/{transcripts,logs}/<sha>-delivery-*` |
+
+## 5. Quality Judgment & Scoring Protocol
+
+Each user-facing story receives independent Functional, Emotional, Trust, and Taste judgments on 0–10 after evidence is eligible. A 5–7 is functional but unproven; 8 is the ceiling for complete captures without a distinct skeptical note; 9 requires that note and no active P0/P1; 10 additionally requires full relevant runtime evidence and no active P0/P1/P2. Current runtime evidence overrides older scorecards. Reusing a skeptical note across dimensions caps each affected score at 8.
+
+## 6. Required Static Evidence
+
+For every UX-RC-or-higher report, store build SHA, sanitized environment, running-build screenshots, browser accessibility-tree output, geometry at 360px/768px/1440px, browser logs with no unhandled exception, and backend/network evidence for each live flow.
+
