+| pulseboard:evidence-contract | `bash .speck/scripts/validation/validate-template.sh specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence-contract.md --strict` | manual | evidence | `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/evidence-contract.md` | `contract_sections>0` | — | — |
+| speck:evidence-citations | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh specs/` | manual | evidence | `specs/**` | `citations>0` | — | — |
+| speck:probe-library | `.speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-evidence-citations.sh --check-probe-library` | manual | evidence | `specs/projects/**` | `probe_classes>0` | — | — |
+
+`manual` is intentional until application CI exists. A gate may move to `pre-commit`, `pre-push`, `commit-msg`, `ci:push`, or `ci:pull_request` only when that hook or CI configuration actually invokes it. A proposed canary must be a reviewed Speck library key and must fail for the injected defect.
+
+## 7. Required Live-Service Evidence
+
+Before readiness above INTEGRATION-GREEN, run the production-like web build against the real authorization, persistence, and delivery runtime. Capture request/response boundaries, authenticated principal identity (sanitized), write baselines/read-backs, provider outcome, and failure posture. No external service or runtime currently exists in this workspace, so there is no live-service evidence and no higher readiness claim.
+
