+## 8. Readiness Criteria
+
+| State | Required evidence | Blocks advancement |
+|---|---|---|
+| NO-SHIP | Product promises and this proof contract exist. | No application, executable tests, runtime build, or validation report exists. |
+| IMPL-GREEN | Implemented promise paths, non-empty tests, mutation evidence for guards, and no unresolved implementation P0/P1. | Any promise without an executable path or a red/empty test suite. |
+| INTEGRATION-GREEN | Production-like web build plus real authorization, persistence, and delivery-boundary smoke probes. | Mock-only evidence, no baselined write read-back, or no two-principal isolation probe. |
+| UX-RC | Cold-start facilitator LARP, baked-build AX and geometry evidence, and separate DOES-IT-WORK/IS-IT-GOOD judgments. | Any primary flow unreachable, unadjudicated, or visually/semantically broken. |
+| COMMERCIAL-RC | If paid delivery/reminders are introduced: real entitlement/payment boundary, value-versus-free/DIY/substitute review, and failure posture. | No revenue path currently exists; this state is inapplicable until one is designed. |
+| SHIP-RC | Current production-like evidence, independent audit, no open P0/P1, fresh profile check, and release decision record. | Dev-only evidence, stale proof, or no independent audit. |
+| SHIP | Deployed artifact and post-deploy smoke evidence. | No deployed artifact exists. |
+
+## 9. Evidence Storage
+
+```
+specs/projects/001-pulseboard/
+└── epics/E###-name/stories/S###-name/
+    ├── screenshots/<sha>-<screen>-<width>-<state>.png
+    ├── ax-trees/<sha>-<screen>.json
+    ├── transcripts/<sha>-<persona>-<flow>.md
+    └── logs/<sha>-<flow>.log
+```
+
+Every artifact name begins with the short build SHA. Datastore baseline/read-back and request-boundary records go in `logs/`; independent LARP adjudication goes in `transcripts/`.
+
+## 10. Who Can Mark a Gate Passed
+
+An AI agent may record CORRECT and ON-CONTRACT evidence; an independently motivated evaluator must audit it. FELT-GOOD and TASTE require AI LARP judgment with the owner retaining final aesthetic direction. SHIP-RC and SHIP require an owner release decision. Tier 0 local reversible work may proceed autonomously; Tier 1 merges need verified evidence; Tier 2 staging/public-test actions require recorded approval; Tier 3 production deployment, production data alteration, payment charging, and real-user communications require recorded human approval and SHIP-RC or higher.
+
+## 11. Adversarial Probe Suite
+
+The suite prompts an adversary; it never defines done. Log each attempt and its observed outcome.
+
+| Probe | Expected behavior |
+|---|---|
+| Missing or altered confirmation field | Scheduling is refused and no reminder row or provider call is created. |
+| Cross-workspace identifier/list/polling attempt | Other-workspace transcript, action, and delivery status remain invisible. |
+| Concurrent confirmation replay | Exactly one delivery record/event or a truthful single terminal failure state. |
+| Delivery provider timeout or rejection | Bounded retry/failure behaviour; never a silent or permanently ambiguous pending state. |
+| Auth header missing or malformed | Stable refusal, never data leakage or 500. |
+| Oversized or malformed action payload | Clear rejection, never partial schedule/write. |
+| Browser narrow-width and keyboard/screen-reader walk | Confirmation fields and primary action remain reachable, visible, and non-overlapping. |
+| Evaluator-tampering scan | No validation/harness alteration makes a no-op change pass. |
+
+## 11a. Standard Probe Library
+
+The closed library is retained without alteration. These exceptions are honest: this repository contains only product artifacts, no runtime, delivery system, migration, external-service integration, or generated/AI surface. Each exception must be replaced by a typed admissible discharge artifact when that capability is introduced.
+
+| Probe ID | Class | Claim type | Admissible substrate | Required negative controls | Discharge artifact | Exception |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| PROBE:provenance | P1 | `behaviour` | render site + generator stamp + the prompt's own exemplars, judged control-vs-treatment on the composed prompt with the shipped model | rendered-with-degraded-provenance · exemplar re-read (deleting the exemplar must not leave the test green) | — | n/a:no generative surface or shipped model exists |
+| PROBE:honest-label | P2 | `persistence` | the write's observed outcome read back out of the datastore against a pre-walk baseline | total-failure render · partial-failure render · the three renders differ | — | n/a:no datastore or write path exists |
+| PROBE:second-actor | P3 | `visibility` | A writes, teardown, B signs in on the same install, offline — once per enumerated persistence layer | signOut vs deleteAccount compared field-for-field · launch-with-data-and-no-owner-record | — | n/a:no authentication or persistence layer exists |
+| PROBE:money-path | P4 | `acceptance` | the real engine as the applying principal, one run per revenue path | entitlement gate flipped and every revenue path goes red · vendor fixture cited to the vendor's field reference · per-user serialized claim write · one declared fail-posture · bounded worst case per tap | — | n/a:no revenue path or payment engine exists |
+| PROBE:named-clock | P5 | `correctness` | an AST/lint rule over write handlers, cache fills and fixtures, plus the date-sensitive suites run under two timezones | a non-UTC TZ run · allowlist entries that name the audience | — | n/a:no code, fixtures, or scheduled worker exists |
+| PROBE:geometry-ax | P6 | `fit` | a baked build: platform AX dump plus container-vs-content geometry at 3 or more widths, numbers in the artifact | adjacent-target overlap · expected-cell presence · page overflow | — | n/a:no baked UI build exists |
+| PROBE:substrate | P7 | `correctness` | §2b parity of this contract against Speck's compiled admissibility table | the parity run reports CITATION_TABLE_PARITY over a non-empty row set | — | n/a:no implemented claim evidence exists; contract parity is checked in this phase |
+| PROBE:migration-dirt | P8 | `acceptance` | the migration applied forward on a throwaway seeded to the target's real dirty shape | pre-state REJECTED · boundary cases still refuse · one migration head after the merge | — | n/a:no migration or datastore exists |
+
+## 12. Stale-Proof Policy
+
+Evidence is fresh only when tied to HEAD or fewer than seven days of commits behind it. Evidence more than 14 days or commits behind the changed subject is stale and cannot support readiness; `/speck-recheck` must rerun it.
+
+## 13. Surrogate Proof Rule
+
+If a report cites invalid or stale evidence, it labels the claim **Surrogate Proof**, refuses UX-RC or higher, names the missing canonical proof, and creates a follow-up at the owning story. Incremental-cache output cannot support UX-RC or higher.
+
+## 14. LARP Runway & Efficiency Controls
+
+Every LARP records build SHA, browser/build identifier, and backend fingerprint. Reuse is allowed only for focused work when that fingerprint is unchanged. UX-RC or higher requires a freshly compiled production build with incremental caches cleared.
